From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: smd-rpm: sm6115: take back the handover's sleep
 votes on XO and QDSS

clk_smd_rpm_handoff() votes every clock of the SoC on in the active set
and in the sleep set. A sleep set vote goes away again only when a
consumer unprepares the clock, so a clock nobody ever prepares keeps it
for good. On SM6115 that is the QDSS clock: its only consumers are the
CoreSight nodes, all disabled. With it on in the APSS sleep set the RPM
does not shut XO down while the APSS sleeps, and the SoC never reaches
its lowest power state in suspend.

Send a zero sleep set vote for the two-set XO and QDSS clocks of SM6115
straight after the handover, each with its own resource id and key. A
consumer that prepares one of them later votes it into the sleep set
again, as before. The active set votes are not touched.

The vendor driver hands the clocks over the same way and then drops the
vote of every clock without a consumer, in both sets: its clocks carry
CLK_ENABLE_HAND_OFF, and the clock framework unprepares what is still
unused at late init (msm-4.19 clk-smd-rpm.c clk_smd_rpm_handoff(), clk.c
clk_unprepare_unused_subtree()). Mainline never got that second half.
Posted for the sibling QCM2290 and not merged: "clk: qcom: smd-rpm: Skip
proxy votes on clocks for QCM2290" (Imran Shaik, 2026-09-10), which
leaves the handover of these clocks out altogether; its review asked for
a disable vote after the handover instead (Stephan Gerhold).

Limited to SM6115, the only SoC it was run on: seventeen of the other
tables vote QDSS with the STATE key, and a board may live on a handover
vote. For XO the same zero is written once more when the critical
active-only XO clock is prepared at registration.

Measured on the MANGMI Air X, 7.3.5, in a build that also had every XO
consumer on the active-only clock: vmin in 5 of 5 suspends, for the
whole sleep, with one APSS shutdown and one XO shutdown per suspend.
The builds without it reached vmin in 0 of 23.
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c | 40 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c
@@ -183,6 +183,14 @@
 	const struct clk_smd_rpm ** const icc_clks;
 	size_t num_icc_clks;
 	bool scaling_before_handover;
+
+	/*
+	 * Clocks whose sleep set vote from the handover is taken back at once.
+	 * Nothing else would do it: a clock that gets no consumer is never
+	 * unprepared.
+	 */
+	const struct clk_smd_rpm ** const sleep_unvote_clks;
+	size_t num_sleep_unvote_clks;
 };
 
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(rpm_smd_clk_lock);
@@ -210,6 +218,19 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int clk_smd_rpm_sleep_unvote(const struct clk_smd_rpm *r)
+{
+	struct clk_smd_rpm_req req = {
+		.key = cpu_to_le32(r->rpm_key),
+		.nbytes = cpu_to_le32(sizeof(u32)),
+		.value = cpu_to_le32(0),
+	};
+
+	return qcom_rpm_smd_write(rpmcc_smd_rpm, QCOM_SMD_RPM_SLEEP_STATE,
+				  r->rpm_res_type, r->rpm_clk_id, &req,
+				  sizeof(req));
+}
+
 static int clk_smd_rpm_set_rate_active(struct clk_smd_rpm *r,
 				       unsigned long rate)
 {
@@ -1211,11 +1232,22 @@
 	[RPM_SMD_RF_CLK2_A_PIN] = &clk_smd_rpm_rf_clk2_a_pin,
 };
 
+/*
+ * Nothing has these two prepared at the handover. Left on in the sleep set,
+ * they keep the RPM from shutting XO down while the APSS sleeps.
+ */
+static const struct clk_smd_rpm *sm6115_sleep_unvote_clks[] = {
+	&clk_smd_rpm_branch_bi_tcxo,
+	&clk_smd_rpm_branch_qdss_clk,
+};
+
 static const struct rpm_smd_clk_desc rpm_clk_sm6115 = {
 	.clks = sm6115_clks,
 	.num_clks = ARRAY_SIZE(sm6115_clks),
 	.icc_clks = sm_qnoc_icc_clks,
-	.num_icc_clks = ARRAY_SIZE(sm_qnoc_icc_clks)
+	.num_icc_clks = ARRAY_SIZE(sm_qnoc_icc_clks),
+	.sleep_unvote_clks = sm6115_sleep_unvote_clks,
+	.num_sleep_unvote_clks = ARRAY_SIZE(sm6115_sleep_unvote_clks),
 };
 
 static struct clk_smd_rpm *sm6375_clks[] = {
@@ -1372,6 +1404,12 @@
 			continue;
 
 		ret = clk_smd_rpm_handoff(desc->icc_clks[i]);
+		if (ret)
+			goto err;
+	}
+
+	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_sleep_unvote_clks; i++) {
+		ret = clk_smd_rpm_sleep_unvote(desc->sleep_unvote_clks[i]);
 		if (ret)
 			goto err;
 	}
